extends ./layout/layout-default
block content
  article.TextPage
    p.Eyebrow BEFORE YOUR FIRST SHIFT
    h1 How to play
    ol.PlaySteps
      li Shortlist 3 people in the first round, 5 in the next, and 8 in the last. A round ends when you reach its target, run out of CVs, or run out of time.
      li Start with six available CVs. The next rounds have ten and fourteen. Choose a person in the office or use Previous and Next to open a CV.
      li Read their skill, experience, academy, and city.
      li Choose Shortlist or Pass. You can also press S or P. Arrow keys switch CVs. Take your time in round one. You get 45 seconds in each later round. Missing a target does not block the story.
      li Open the engineer's email. Send the reviewed CV file, peek at the old records and choose which ones Scout should learn from.
      li Run the scanner. Open Maya's message, find the named applicant in the inspector and reply.
      li Compare the city results and reopen the case. Change only city or academy on a copy and choose Scan both.
      li Choose Hide city or Learn from work tests. Try either repair on the same 80 practice CVs.
      li Lock one repair and see the results for 200 fresh CVs. Open an example to see both decisions and the work test result. Watching the sample scans is optional.
      li Click Continue to recap. Then explore your own run in the interactive case notes or skip to your audit receipt.
    p Use Pause or press Esc to take a break. Switching tabs pauses the game. You can reload and continue a saved shift.
    h2 What will you learn?
    p A model can learn to repeat old choices, including their mistakes. Run an experiment and use a fresh batch to see whether a repair helps.
    a.MainButton(href='./game/') Start your shift
